"A remark on optimal weighted Poincaré inequalities for convex domains (https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0680)\nciteturn5academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.3 years ago; Authors: Vincenzo Ferone, Carlo Nitsch, Cristina Trombetti ... We prove a sharp upper bound on convex domains, in terms of the diameter alone, of the best constant in a class of weighted Poincar\\'e inequalities.The key point is the study of an optimal weighted Wirtinger inequality.\nTitle: A remark on optimal weighted Poincaré inequalities for convex domains\nAuthors: Vincenzo Ferone, Carlo Nitsch, Cristina Trombetti\nDate: Tue Jul  3 13:56:00 2012\n\nWe prove a sharp upper bound on convex domains, in terms of the diameter alone, of the best constant in a class of weighted Poincar\\'e inequalities. The key point is the study of an optimal weighted Wirtinger inequality.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBest constants in Poincaré inequalities for convex domains (https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.2960)\nciteturn5academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 15.0 years ago; Nitsch, C.Trombetti ... We prove a Payne-Weinberger type inequality for the $p$-Laplacian Neumann eigenvalues ($p\\ge 2$).The inequality provides the sharp upper bound on convex domains, in terms of the diameter alone, of the best constants in Poincar\\'e inequality.\nTitle: Best constants in Poincaré inequalities for convex domains\nAuthors: L. Esposito, C. Nitsch, C. Trombetti\nDate: Thu Oct 13 14:33:57 2011\n\nWe prove a Payne-Weinberger type inequality for the $p$-Laplacian Neumann eigenvalues ($p\\ge 2$). The inequality provides the sharp upper bound on convex domains, in terms of the diameter alone, of the best constants in Poincar\\'e inequality. The key point is the implementation of a refinement of the classical P\\'olya-Szeg\\\"o inequality for the symmetric decreasing rearrangement which yields an optimal weighted Wirtinger inequality.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA REMARK ON OPTIMAL WEIGHTED POINCAR´E (https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=fda56fb5d5b930f76450ae02d8e89ce5314df8d8&repid=rep1&type=pdf)\nciteturn5search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; INEQUALITIES FOR CONVEX DOMAINS ... TROMBETTI∗ ... terms of the diameter alone, of the best constant in a class of weighted ... Wirtinger inequality. ... email: ferone@unina.it; c.nitsch@unina.it; cristina@unina.it.\nA REMARK ON OPTIMAL WEIGHTED POINCAR´E\nINEQUALITIES FOR CONVEX DOMAINS\nV. FERONE∗- C. NITSCH∗- C. TROMBETTI∗\nAbstract. We prove a sharp upper bound on convex domains, in\nterms of the diameter alone, of the best constant in a class of weighted\nPoincar´e inequalities. The key point is the study of an optimal weighted\nWirtinger inequality.\n1. Introduction\nIt is well known that (see for instance [21]), for any given open bounded\nLipschitz connected set Ω, a Poincar´e inequality holds true, in the sense\nthat there exists a positive constant CΩ,p such that\n(1.1)\ninf\nt∈R ∥u −t∥Lp(Ω) ≤CΩ,p∥Du∥Lp(Ω),\nfor all Lipschitz functions u in Ω.\nThe value of the best constant in (1.1) is the reciprocal of the ﬁrst non-\ntrivial Neumann eigenvalue of the p-Laplacian over Ω. In [23] (see also [2]),\nit has been proved that, if p = 2, and Ωis convex, in any dimension\n\u0012Z\n2\nΩ\n|Du|2\n\u0013 1\n\u0012Z\nd ,\n2\n≥π\n(1.2)\n1\nCΩ,2\n=\nmin\nu∈H1(Ω)\nR\nΩu=0\nΩ\n|u|2\n\u0013 1\narXiv:1207.0680v2  [math.OC]  6 Nov 2012\nwhere d is the diameter of Ω. Observe that the last term of (1.2) is exactly\nthe value achieved, in dimension n = 1 on any interval of length d, by\nthe ﬁrst nontrivial Laplacian eigenvalue (without distinction between the\nNeumann and the Dirichlet conditions).\nKey words and phrases. Poincar´e inequalities, p-Laplacian eigenvalues, Wirtinger\ninequalities.\n∗Dipartimento di Matematica e Applicazioni “R. Caccioppoli”, Universit`a degli Studi\ndi Napoli Federico II, Complesso Monte S. Angelo, via Cintia - 801